> diff sin(fma(x,x,x))
d/dx sin(fma(x, x, x)) = 2x*cos(fma(x, x, x)) + cos(fma(x, x, x))
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 4e-10)
> diff fma(x,x,x)
d/dx fma(x, x, x) = 2x + 1
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> diff fma(x,y,z)
  note: fma(x, y, z) has 3 variables (x, y, z): all first partial derivatives, the gradient (say `diff F x` for one)
∇ fma(x, y, z) = (y, x, 1)
  ∂/∂x fma(x, y, z) = y
  ∂/∂y fma(x, y, z) = x
  ∂/∂z fma(x, y, z) = 1
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 300 points (max relative difference 3e-13)
> diff exp(fma(x,x,x))
d/dx exp(fma(x, x, x)) = 2x*exp(fma(x, x, x)) + exp(fma(x, x, x))
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 4e-10)
